20260919120000000508,20260919120000000508,index a rear derailleur,20260919120000000506
20260919120000000509,20260919120000000508,applies to,20260919120000000131
20260919120000000510,20260919120000000508,tools,a 5 mm hex key and a screwdriver, nothing else
20260919120000000511,20260919120000000508,tell,The chain hesitates going up the block, or rattles once it is there
20260919120000000512,20260919120000000508,how,Slack the cable, set the limit screws, take up the slack, then quarter turns of the barrel adjuster until it is quiet
20260919120000000513,20260919120000000508,interval,whenever a new cable settles, then rarely
20260919120000000514,20260919120000000514,patch a tube,20260919120000000506
20260919120000000515,20260919120000000514,tools,tyre levers, patches, glue, and a pump that actually reaches pressure
20260919120000000516,20260919120000000514,tell,A tyre that is soft again the morning after you pumped it
20260919120000000517,20260919120000000514,how,Find the hole, sand it dull, thin layer of glue, wait until it is tacky rather than wet, press the patch hard for a minute
20260919120000000518,20260919120000000514,note,Run the inside of the tyre with a finger first, or you will patch it twice
20260919120000000519,20260919120000000519,true a wheel,20260919120000000506
20260919120000000520,20260919120000000519,tools,a spoke key, and a truing stand if you have one, brake pads if you do not
20260919120000000521,20260919120000000519,tell,The rim brushes one pad once a revolution
20260919120000000522,20260919120000000519,how,Find the high side, loosen the spoke that pulls that way a quarter turn, tighten its neighbour the same, work in small passes
20260919120000000523,20260919120000000519,note,Stress relieve the wheel afterwards or it will go out again on the first ride
20260919120000000524,20260919120000000524,bleed a hydraulic disc brake,20260919120000000506
20260919120000000525,20260919120000000524,applies to,20260919120000000134
20260919120000000526,20260919120000000524,tools,a bleed kit for that brand, and the right fluid, which is not interchangeable
20260919120000000527,20260919120000000524,tell,The lever pulls closer to the bar than it used to, or feels spongy at the end
20260919120000000528,20260919120000000524,interval,once a year, or whenever the lever goes soft
